{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/842373-packing-for-a-vampire-road-trip","id":842373,"title":"Packing for a vampire road trip","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T20:11:10-08:00","id":842373,"title":"Packing for a vampire road trip","content":"So, assume you're a vampire. And you need to take a fairly long trip. What do you pack? What form of transport do you take? What kind of vehicle? Who do you bring? Other vampires, ghouls, humans? A Mage who owes you big? <br /> <br /> If you're wealthy and influential, what do you do? If you're moderately well off? What about if you're penniless and the target of a blood hunt?<br /> <br /> Note: Assume for the purpose of this exercise that &quot;just don't go&quot; isn't an option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T20:39:13-08:00","id":842384,"title":"","content":"I'd probably just take a ghoul and a blood doll or two. Entering another domain and feeding is just asking for trouble, someone's going to act like you poached their territory or you'll provoke the wrath of some unknown supernatural or something else horrible. Obviously the most common form of transport would be a car. Have your ghoul drive during the day with you bundled in the trunk. They did this in the movie <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Forsaken_(film)\" target=\"_blank\">the Forsaken</a>. In that and other movies traveling vampires tend to pick up hitchhikers, prostitutes, other travelers who can disappear off the face of the Earth without anyone noticing for a while, by which point they're long gone anyways. There's a book specifically about vampires who travel, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/1590/Nomads\" target=\"_blank\">Nomads</a>. Chapter three has a lot of advice about the subject.<br /> <br /> A plane would be ideal. There's a character in Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners with a private plane who transports vampires safely. With a plane you can make a lot of distance in a little time, ending up across the country in certain directions and landing with night-time to spare. If it's a private plane you can be sure the windows won't be opened and sunlight isn't a risk at all.<br /> <br /> If you have no money and need to get out of there, just use a car or run. Stealing a car is pretty easy for vampires, but if you can't even do that, on foot you have a lot more room to maneuver, even if you'll be making ground much slower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T21:02:52-08:00","id":842391,"title":"","content":"If I have some money and don't mind being relatively traceable I get a ghoul to rent a U-Haul, stick myself in a box inside the U-Haul's trailer, and make a wall between said box and the door with other boxes full of needed supplies.<br /> <br /> If I don't, I better hope I have Protean 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T08:13:34-08:00","id":842570,"title":"","content":"Protean 3 is great if you are penniless. You can turn into a wolf and run all night long. If you are low Blood Potency, you can also feed on animals. Protean 1 helps you to stay safe from the sun. Gangrels are very good at living/travel in the wild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Homebrews:</span></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1492909-horodrigo-homebrews-2ed\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Vampire Homebrews</b></span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Mage Legacies:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1074696-2ed-legacy-experiment-infernal-ones\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal Ones</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070254-2e-legacies-conversions-and-homebrew?p=1078103#post1078103\" target=\"_blank\">Daoine</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1536102-homebrew-legacy-the-changed\" target=\"_blank\">Changed</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7210-horodrigo","name":"Horodrigo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T08:11:02-08:00","id":842989,"title":"","content":"Absolutely imperative is to bring your own snacks. The more you have to go out hunting in unfamiliar territory the more exposed you are and the more likely you are to run afoul of local supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}